#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# permutation_cycle_type

#% text
# `permutation_cycle_type(p), (p, n)`: the cycle lengths in decreasing order (with fixed points up to n)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Without n, the lengths of the cycles of length at least 2; with n, every cycle on 1, ..., n, fixed points as 1.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
permutation_cycle_type(cycles([[1, 2, 3], [5, 6]]))
#% output
#= [3, 2]

#% cell
permutation_cycle_type(cycles([[1, 2, 3], [5, 6]]), 7)
#% output
#= [3, 2, 1, 1]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `permutation_order`, `permutation_sign`
